#!/usr/bin/env python
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
r"""
AP1 - the approval panel: two kinds of condition, and a push to the Chief.

RULING (2026-08-15): the bank credit analyst may "approve with pre-approval
conditions, pre-disbursement conditions, return for additional documentation or
information, or push to the Chief Credit Risk for their approval as well."

I DID NOT BUILD A NEW PANEL. ActionPanelDecision already carried verdict,
authority, reason, conditions and comments, and return-for-information already
existed. What was missing was the second kind of condition and the escalation -
so this extends the panel rather than replacing it. That is the fourth time
this fortnight the answer was "where is it?" rather than "how do I build it?".

TWO CONDITION BOXES, because different people clear them:

    Pre-approval        cleared by credit admin; the last tick releases the
                        case to Trops
    Pre-disbursement    cleared by Trops before money moves

The existing `conditions` field is KEPT AND SENT UNCHANGED alongside the new
pre_approval list. Every decision recorded before today used it that way, and
the server reads it as the fallback - so nothing recorded historically becomes
unconditional.

PUSH TO THE CHIEF asks for a reason and refuses without one: a case arriving on
the Chief's desk with no question attached wastes the trip. THE CHIEF IS
RESOLVED SERVER-SIDE - this screen names nobody, because a bank changes its
people more often than its software. And the case does not change hands; the
toast says so.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, vite build clean.

Usage (from project root, .venv active):
    python scripts\\patch_ap1_approval_panel.py            # dry run
    python scripts\\patch_ap1_approval_panel.py --apply
"""
